WEBVTT

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:33.548
On my travels, I became friends
with the elite young musicians

00:01:33.589 --> 00:01:35.675
who seemed to have all the resources.

00:01:35.716 --> 00:01:37.760
Because they lived
next to musical capitals

00:01:37.802 --> 00:01:40.054
like New York, Chicago or LA,

00:01:40.054 --> 00:01:42.890
they studied at places like Juilliard
on the weekends.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:45.977
They watched their teachers
perform at major symphony orchestras.

00:01:45.977 --> 00:01:49.605
They had access to almost every
musical opportunity that you can imagine

00:01:49.605 --> 00:01:51.274
right in their home communities.

00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:54.735
And even though I was proud
of the hard work that I'd done

00:01:54.735 --> 00:01:56.028
to get to their level,

00:01:56.028 --> 00:01:57.864
I hated always feeling behind

00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:00.241
because I never had access
to private lessons.